+# Extension Lifecycle Documentation Alignment
+
+## Task State
+
+Planned for the user's CLI implementer in a separate chat. Implementation has not started. Keep this record in the Task 28 review worktree until the user authorizes integration. Register a task ID in the [project control ledger](../project-control.md) on activation.
+
+Task 28 separates current Extension concepts from historical MVP details. This task records the remaining CLI documentation work. It does not dispatch an implementer or authorize a behavior change, merge, or publication. Select a fresh accepted implementation baseline after the source review is integrated.
+
+## Outcome
+
+Make current Extension setup and lifecycle instructions easy to find and accurate for their declared CLI version. Keep frozen executable examples and evidence explicitly historical, including when a reader follows a direct section link.
+
+The [Extensions Architecture](../../../crystallized/documents/extensions/architecture.md) defines package meaning and composition. The [MVP archive](../../../archived/extensions-mvp-architecture.md) preserves historical details. CLI contracts define exact representation, operations, permissions, lifecycle state, and recovery.
